WEBVTT

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.480
<v Team Lead>Morning everyone. Can you all hear me ok?</v>

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.350
<v Employee A>Yep, loud and clear.</v>

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.200
<v Employee B>Morning! Yes.</v>

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.400
<v Employee C>Goedemorgen. Yes, I hear you.</v>

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.200
<v Team Lead>Good. How was the weekend? Anyone did something fun?</v>

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.300
<v Employee B>I finally fixed my bike, so, uh, that's my big news.</v>

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.800
<v Employee A>We went to the coast. Freezing, but nice.</v>

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.600
<v Employee C>Has anyone seen that the coffee machine on the third floor is broken again?</v>

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.100
<v Team Lead>Yeah, yeah, facilities knows. Third time this month.</v>

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.200
<v Employee A>We should just get our own machine for the team, honestly.</v>

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.900
<v Team Lead>Ha, put it on the wish list. Ok, let's start.</v>

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:19.200
<v Team Lead>So, main topic today is the November run. I want to make sure we all handle the late invoices the same way.</v>

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.500
<v Team Lead>Let's do the usual round. A, anything from your side first?</v>

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:33.600
<v Employee A>Yeah, a couple of things. I had three contractors last month who sent their invoice on the twenty-eighth and still expected to be paid in the same run.</v>

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.700
<v Employee A>And we did it, but it was, uh, a lot of manual work at the end.</v>

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.100
<v Team Lead>Mm-hmm.</v>

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.600
<v Employee A>Two of the three are closed now, the third one is waiting for a corrected invoice.</v>

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.000
<v Team Lead>Ok, thanks. B?</v>

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:53.900
<v Employee B>Uh, from my side it's mostly onboarding questions, I'll keep them for the end.</v>

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.000
<v Team Lead>Fine. C?</v>

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.200
<v Employee C>All good, I processed the October invoices, no surprises.</v>

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:21.400
<v Team Lead>Before the cut-off, a quick look at the open cases. We have eleven open, which is a bit much.</v>

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.300
<v Employee A>Most of them are waiting for documents from the contractors.</v>

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.900
<v Employee B>Should we send a reminder?</v>

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:33.100
<v Team Lead>Yes, let's take that as an action at the end.</v>

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:45.600
<v Employee C>One of mine is waiting for the client to approve the timesheet, that's out of our hands.</v>

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.000
<v Team Lead>Ok, fine.</v>

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:30.200
<v Team Lead>Ok. A, you handle most of the contractor invoices, you wanted to explain the cut-off.</v>

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:37.800
<v Employee A>Right. So anything that comes in after the twentieth — no, sorry, the twenty-fifth — goes into next month's run.</v>

00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.600
<v Employee B>Mm-hmm, ok.</v>

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:45.500
<v Employee C>Yes, that's right, it was in the payroll newsletter in September.</v>

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:51.400
<v Employee A>Exactly. So for the November run, if it arrives on the twenty-sixth, it's December.</v>

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.200
<v Employee B>And what if the contractor says it's urgent?</v>

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:01.300
<v Team Lead>Let's wait for the Manager for that one, it was agreed with Finance.</v>

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:34.000
<v Manager>Hi all, sorry, I'm late. The previous meeting ran over.</v>

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:40.600
<v Team Lead>No problem, we're at the cut-off. B asked about urgent invoices.</v>

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:13.400
<v Team Lead>So, an urgent invoice after the cut-off can still be paid, but only with my approval by e-mail before the run is closed.</v>

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:19.200
<v Team Lead>No e-mail, no off-cycle payment. Otherwise we're back to the chaos of last month.</v>

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.400
<v Manager>Yes, that's how we agreed it with Finance.</v>

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.300
<v Employee B>Ok, clear.</v>

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.400
<v Employee A>Good, that makes it much easier to say no.</v>

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.000
<v Team Lead>Exactly.</v>

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:51.300
<v Employee B>One more thing from my side. Since the fake invoice at the Antwerp team last month, Finance asked everyone to check a new contractor's VAT number in vies before the first payment.</v>

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:57.100
<v Employee B>It takes like one minute, you just enter the number on the European site.</v>

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:01.200
<v Team Lead>Good point. Did everyone hear about that fake invoice?</v>

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.300
<v Employee C>Yes, scary.</v>

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:04.900
<v Employee A>Mm-hmm.</v>

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:20.400
<v Employee B>Oh, and does the cut-off also apply to Luxembourg contractors? We have two now.</v>

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:23.600
<v Team Lead>Good question, no idea, let's check.</v>

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:26.200
<v Employee A>I'm not sure either.</v>

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.800
<v Team Lead>Ok, let's move on.</v>

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:04.600
<v Team Lead>Ok, action items. C, can you update the checklist by Friday?</v>

00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:06.100
<v Employee C>Sure.</v>

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:11.800
<v Team Lead>B, send the reminder to the contractors with open documents.</v>

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.200
<v Employee B>Will do.</v>

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:43.300
<v Team Lead>Ok, thanks all, see you next week.</v>

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:45.200
<v Manager>Thanks, bye.</v>

00:29:45.400 --> 00:29:46.300
<v Employee A>Bye!</v>
